capability wkt/timestamp  a Timestamp to and from an instant, and its RFC 3339 text
  heroes  protobuf.from_instant, protobuf.to_instant, protobuf.format_timestamp, protobuf.parse_timestamp
  go      timestamppb.New, timestamppb.Now, timestamppb.Timestamp.AsTime, timestamppb.Timestamp.CheckValid, timestamppb.Timestamp.IsValid
  rust    prost_types::Timestamp, prost_types::TimestampError
  python  timestamp_pb2.Timestamp.FromDatetime, ToDatetime, FromJsonString, ToJsonString, GetCurrentTime, FromSeconds, ToSeconds, FromMilliseconds, ToMilliseconds, FromMicroseconds, ToMicroseconds, FromNanoseconds, ToNanoseconds
  note    the text spans 0001 to 9999 as the type does, wider than a `time.Instant`, which `to_instant` fails `does_not_fit` past; 0, 3, 6 or 9 fraction digits as Go writes them. Now is `from_instant(time.now()?)`; seconds and their parts are `time`'s

capability wkt/duration  a Duration to and from a `time.Duration`, and its text
  heroes  protobuf.from_duration, protobuf.to_duration, protobuf.format_duration, protobuf.parse_duration
  go      durationpb.New, durationpb.Duration.AsDuration, durationpb.Duration.CheckValid, durationpb.Duration.IsValid
  rust    prost_types::Duration, prost_types::DurationError
  python  duration_pb2.Duration.FromTimedelta, ToTimedelta, FromJsonString, ToJsonString, FromSeconds, ToSeconds, FromMilliseconds, ToMilliseconds, FromMicroseconds, ToMicroseconds, FromNanoseconds, ToNanoseconds
